"""patch_phase153a.py -- V153: the WebGPU engine, WebGL kept (Render R2).

- The V152 description of the scene is now the engines' common part (bimSceneSync): the chunks'
  arrays, the object table, the rebuilds. Each engine keeps its own GPU copies and its own record
  of the table rows it has yet to receive.
- WebGPU, where the browser has it: started asynchronously when 3D is first drawn (WebGL draws
  meanwhile); WGSL shaders doing what V152's do; the chunks as vertex buffers, the table as a
  storage buffer; 4x multisampling as WebGL's antialias; every draw recorded once in a render
  bundle, replayed each frame with only the camera's matrices sent, recorded again only when a
  chunk is rebuilt, the table grows or the passes change.
- WebGL draws when WebGPU is missing, failed, lost, starting, or not chosen (GRAPHICS), and for a
  frame with the map or a terrain surface in 3D, which WebGPU does not draw yet (Render R3).
- GRAPHICS switches between WebGPU-where-available and WebGL, kept in this browser; Statistics
  shows which engine drew the last frame."""
